title: "BLEECAM™ (Benchmarking Life Cycle Environmental, Economic, and Social Metrics for Critical and Advanced Minerals and Materials) [SWR-25-125]"
abstract: >-
  BLEECAM is an open-source, integrated decision-support tool for evaluating the
  impacts, risks, and trade-offs across U.S. and global materials supply chains. It
  integrates multi-objective supply-chain optimization, system dynamics, network
  design, life-cycle assessment (LCA), techno-economic modeling (TEA/LCC), and social
  impact assessment (S-LCA) to evaluate how supply chains evolve over time, geography,
  and deployment scenarios. Developed at the National Laboratory of the Rockies (NLR)
  with funding from the U.S. Department of Energy's Office of Critical Minerals and
  Energy Innovation (CMEI) and Advanced Materials and Manufacturing Technologies
  Office (AMMTO).
